    "proof": "Put pi=sqrt(2), rho=2*pi-1 and delta=(1+pi)*rho=3+pi. For a primitive root r=(x,y), reflection integrality says q(r)|2I(r), I(r)=(rho*x,(y,Lambda25)). The Smith form 1,1,2^22,16 has largest pi-primary exponent 8. Evenness excludes v_pi(q)=1. If v_pi(q)=e>2, then x is divisible by pi^(e-2) and G*y by pi^(e-2); e>10 would make both x and y divisible by pi. Thus the complete dyadic valuations are 0 and 2 through 10. For y=u+pi*v, writing k=e-2 gives the exact gates G*u=0 mod 2^ceil(k/2) and G*v=0 mod 2^floor(k/2). Away from pi and the coefficient prime, local unimodularity excludes every prime. At delta the exponent is zero or one; in the latter case y lies in delta*Lambda25. The choices are independent. Class number one and U^+=U^2 give the twenty canonical generators obtained from 1,2,4+2*pi,4,8+4*pi,8,16+8*pi,16,32+16*pi,32 with an optional factor delta."
  },
